    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Dooley Auctioneers has the great pleasure to present Aenbarr to the market. Situated on a very private c. 0.5 acre site surrounded by mature trees and flowering plants and including a lovely private driveway, this charming detached country cottage is perfectly positioned on the foot of the Sugarloaf mountain and within minutes from Kilmacanogue village.\r\n\r\nThe spacious accommodation, measuring over 220 sq. m or 2,377 sq. ft, comprises an entrance hallway, with two rooms on each side of the hall leading into the living/dining room, country kitchen and conservatory. To the rear of the property lies three well-proportioned double bedrooms, with the master bedroom containing an ensuite. A family bathroom completes the ground floor accommodation. On the first floor, there are a further three bedrooms, two double and one single.\r\n\r\nThe property dates back to 1930 owned by the Attorney General during W.W.II and hosts an array of its original features with some modern additions made over the years. The private and mature gardens surrounding the house are a dream come true to any gardener and will appeal to many who love the outdoors. The original house was built in the 1930s . It was extended in 1977 and 1986. The extension has 5 bedrooms and 2 bathrooms. Part of the older part of the house is now a self-contained flat, with a double bedroom and its own small back garden.\r\n\r\nThe gardens are a particular highlight. Mature planting, established trees and flowering borders create a wonderfully private setting, with ample space for outdoor dining, relaxing and gardening. The grounds provide an attractive backdrop to the house throughout the seasons and will particularly appeal to those seeking space and a connection to the outdoors. The Sugarloaf walking trail is accessible directly from the driveway entrance, offering a scenic route to the mountain.\r\n\r\nAenbarr enjoys a convenient location that combines countryside surroundings with access to nearby towns and transport links. Kilmacanogue village is within easy reach just a few minutes walk, while Bray, Enniskerry and Greystones offer a wide choice of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants and leisure amenities. The N11 provides access towards Dublin and the M50, with DART services available from Bray and Luas services from Cherrywood.\r\n\r\nWith its character, extensive accommodation and mature private grounds, Aenbarr presents an opportunity to acquire a distinctive family home in a scenic and accessible setting.\r\n\r\nViewing is an absolute must to really see what Aenbarr has to offer."
      },
      {
